<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech June real retail sales up 5.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Czech June real retail sales up 5.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech real retail sales rose 5.0 percent year-on-year in June, putting retail sales in the first half of 1997 3.5 percent higher than in the same period last year, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Monday.  </p>
<p> TOTAL REAL RETAIL SALES    JUNE 97  MAY 97     JAN-JUNE</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 5.0     3.1	   3.5</p>
<p>Sales, repairs of motor</p>
<p> vehicles			   17.5     8.1	   9.5</p>
<p> Sales of fuels		   15.6     9.2	  11.1</p>
<p>Retail sales including</p>
<p> repairs to consumer goods     0.4     3.1	   1.0</p>
<p>Restaurants and</p>
<p> accommodation		    -1.6    -3.7	  -3.9</p>
<p>TRANSPORT   TOTAL		  7.0    -1.7	  -1.8</p>
<p>  railways			   2.4   -10.6	  -6.0</p>
<p>  road transport		   4.6    -3.6	  -1.3</p>
<p>  river			     30.0     0.5	  -2.9</p>
<p>  air				 14.3    10.9	   5.0</p>
<p>parallel and support activities</p>
<p>					13.3     8.4	   2.3</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are preliminary. Total retail sales include the sale and repair of motor vehicles and sales of fuels.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
